  "verbalization": "Cilazapril, a drug indicated for hypertension, is linked to Hypertensive Disorder through a series of intermediate medications that share a common pathway of action. The evidence suggests that Cilazapril is classified under the category of antihypertensive agents, which are used to treat hypertension, and that this class of drugs is associated with Hypertensive Disorder. The presence of multiple pathways—each involving a different antihypertensive medication—indicates that Cilazapril may exert its effects through mechanisms that are broadly relevant to the treatment of hypertension, thereby contributing to the development of Hypertensive Disorder. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of antihypertensive drugs in the pathophysiology of hypertension and its related conditions. The evidence supports a mechanism of action that is both general and specific, aligning with the observed clinical associations.",
